### prompt variable expands on the client side
ssh backup01 "echo $PS1"
>>> SC2029 1:20

### pure literal remote command is fine
ssh backup01 "ls foo"
>>> none

### only a host argument
ssh "$target_host"
>>> SC2154 1:6

### an identity option disables the check
ssh -i ~/.ssh/deploy_ed25519 "$target_host"
>>> SC2154 1:31

### a function's local variable cannot exist on the server
#!/bin/bash
f() {
  local value
  value=$(date)
  ssh host "echo '$value'"
}
f
>>- SC2029 5:19 -- the name is local to this function, so expanding it here is the only way the server can see its value
